# More debate scenes, all realms. Each keeps arguments players made in 2001-2003 (research brief
# section 7, period knowledge unless marked) in new words. Roles are different bots of one realm.

@kind debate
@realm *

@topic realm_abilities
@levels 40-50
@scene first_realm_ability
@role B type=NoLifer
@role C type=Daredevil,Leveler
@role D type=*
A: {q} first realm ability, what is everyone buying?
B: purge. a stun or mez you can shrug off wins more fights than anything
C: purge is pricey for a first pick, cheap passives add up faster
B: passives do not help when you are mezzed for half the fight
D: depends on the class, a caster wants different things than a tank
C: true, my healer friend swears by mastery of concentration
B: cast through the hits, sure, still buying purge first
A: ok so the answer is it depends. classic

@topic group_setup
@levels 35-50
@scene group_setup
@role B type=NoLifer
@role C type=Socialite,Leveler
@role D type=Daredevil
A: whats the ideal 8man, honestly?
B: two healers, a mezzer, a speed class, a tank, and damage for the rest
C: that is the dream. in practice you take whoever is online
D: give me four damage classes and one healer, fights end before they start
B: until the other group mezzes your healer and you all fold
D: then we die fast and run back fast, still fun
C: the best group is the one where people actually assist
A: assist. right. who is main assist tonight?

@topic assist
@levels 20-50
@scene assist
@role B type=NoLifer,Leveler
@role C type=Daredevil
A: why does every group fight turn into everyone hitting something different?
B: nobody uses /assist. one target, everyone on it, that is the whole secret
C: i like picking my own targets though
B: and that is why the healer on the other side never dies
C: ok fine, but the main assist better be fast
A: setting up an assist macro right now

@topic mez_breaks
@levels 20-50
@scene mez_breaks
@role B class=Sorcerer,Healer,Bard,Minstrel,Mentalist
@role C type=Daredevil
A: who broke the mez on that last pull?
C: in my defense it was standing right there
B: it was standing there because it was mezzed
C: ok in my defense i did not read the group chat
B: rule one: do not touch the sleeping ones
A: lol. noted for the next pull

@topic pulling
@levels 20-50
@scene pulling
@role B type=Leveler
@role C type=Daredevil
@role D type=Socialite
A: can we agree only one person pulls tonight?
B: yes please, two pullers means double the adds
C: but the puller is slow, i can grab the next one while they kill this
B: and then the healer runs out of power and we all lie down
D: the puller sets the pace, everyone else enjoys the ride
C: fine, i will just stand here looking impatient
A: perfect, thank you

@topic named_drops
@levels 30-50
@scene named_camping
@role B type=Leveler,NoLifer
@role C type=Crafter
@role D type=Explorer
A: camping a named for a drop for three hours now, worth it?
B: a good named drop beats anything you can buy at that level
C: or i could make you something just as good in an evening
B: crafted has no procs. that drop has a proc
C: the proc fires once a fight and you paid three hours for it
D: i like the hunt itself, the drop is a bonus
A: one more hour. then i call a crafter

@topic dragons
@levels 45-50
@scene dragon_raid
@role B type=NoLifer,Daredevil
@role C type=Socialite
@role D type=Leveler
A: anyone going on the dragon raid this weekend?
B: of course, the whole realm shows up for the dragon
C: last time half the raid died to the first breath
D: is it even worth it? hundreds of people and one loot table
B: it is not about the loot, it is about being there when it falls
C: and the stories after, those are the best part
D: ok, i will come for the stories
A: bring patience and a healer you trust

@topic housing
@levels 20-50
@scene housing
@role B type=Crafter,Socialite
@role C type=Leveler,NoLifer
A: is a house worth the coin?
B: a house is a home, plus storage, plus somewhere to show off
C: it is a weekly rent bill for a room you visit twice a month
B: decorate it right and your friends will visit too
C: my friends are in the frontier, not in my living room
A: maybe a small cottage to start

@topic alts
@levels 1-50
@scene altitis
@role B type=Explorer,Socialite
@role C type=Leveler,NoLifer
A: i have six alts and none of them past 30. help
B: alts are how you learn the game, every class teaches you something
C: one main to 50 teaches you more than six half-done characters
B: and if you get bored of your main?
C: then you push through, 50 is worth it
A: so the cure for alt-itis is more alt-itis. got it

@topic grey_xp
@levels 1-50
@scene grey_kills
@role B type=Leveler
@role C type=Daredevil
A: is anyone else still killing greys for loot?
B: greys give nothing. yellow and orange, that is where the xp is
C: oranges if you have a healer, reds if you are brave
B: reds if you like your bind point
C: my bind point and i are close friends
A: blues it is, i am a coward

@topic epics
@levels 45-50
@scene epic_armor
@role B type=Leveler,NoLifer
@role C type=Crafter
A: is the epic armor worth the quest?
B: the look alone is worth it, everyone knows you finished the epic
C: the stats get outclassed by a decent crafted suit
B: crafted does not have that look
C: you can dye crafted any color you like
A: i will do the quest for the look and wear crafted for the fights

@topic death_penalty
@levels 20-50
@scene death_penalty
@role B type=Leveler
@role C type=Daredevil
A: lost half a bubble to one death, the penalty is brutal
B: that is why you consider before you pull
C: the penalty is what makes the win feel good
B: easy to say when it is not your xp bar going backwards
C: i have died five times tonight, still smiling
A: you are not well

@topic loot_rules
@levels 20-50
@scene loot_rules
@role B type=Socialite
@role C type=NoLifer
@role D type=*
A: group loot rules tonight? need before greed?
B: need before greed, roll for anything nobody needs
C: random loot is fair, everyone gets the same chance
B: then a caster gets the shield and sells it
C: and the tank buys it off him, everyone wins
D: just do not ninja it and we are fine
A: need before greed it is

@topic leveling_route
@levels 20-34
@scene dungeon_or_outside
@role B type=Leveler
@role C type=Explorer
A: dungeon or outdoor camps for the 20s?
B: dungeons, the camp bonus and the respawns are better
C: outdoors, you can see the adds coming and run if it goes bad
B: running is for people who do not have a mezzer
C: having a mezzer is for people who have friends online
A: outdoor tonight, dungeon this weekend

@topic speed
@levels 20-50
@scene speed_class
@role B class=Skald,Minstrel,Bard
@role C type=*
A: why does every group ask for a speed class first?
B: because walking everywhere is slow and boring
C: and because speed wins the run home after a bad fight
B: i am a speed bot with feelings, remember that
C: a speed bot with feelings and great songs
A: we love you, speed class, never leave

@topic stuns
@levels 35-50
@scene stun_mez_det
@role B type=NoLifer
@role C type=Leveler
A: chain stunned for ten seconds and died without moving
B: determination. it shortens stuns and mez, buy it
C: points spent there are points not spent on damage
B: damage does not help when you cannot move
C: then i will just stay out of stun range
A: buying a little determination, thanks

@topic keep_claims
@levels 40-50
@scene keep_claims
@role B type=NoLifer
@role C type=Socialite
A: our guild claimed {keep}, it actually means something now
B: a claim is a target, every enemy zerg will come for it
C: and every member will show up to defend it, that is the fun
B: until it is 3am and nobody is online
C: then we take it back the next night
A: guild night at {keep}, everyone come

@topic off_hours
@levels 40-50
@scene off_hour_raids
@role B type=Leveler,Socialite
@role C type=NoLifer
A: they took our relic at four am again
B: hitting a keep when nobody is awake is not winning
C: a relic left unguarded is a relic waiting to be taken
B: there is no fight in that, just walking in
C: then guard it. war does not sleep
A: setting an alarm for the next one, apparently

@topic bind_points
@levels 1-50
@scene bind_point
@role B type=Leveler
@role C type=Explorer
A: where does everyone bind?
B: close to your camp, every death is a short walk
C: in town, so i can restock after every death
B: a long run back eats more time than the restock
C: a full bag eats more than both
A: binding next to the merchant then

@topic pets_rvr
@levels 35-50
@scene pet_classes_rvr
@role B class=Bonedancer,Spiritmaster,Theurgist,Cabalist,Necromancer,Enchanter,Druid,Animist,Hunter
@role C type=NoLifer,Daredevil
A: are pet classes any good in the frontier?
C: pets get mezzed, rooted, killed, then the owner is alone
B: or they soak hits while i cast from safety
C: a smart group kills the owner first
B: a smart owner stays behind the group
A: so it depends on the owner. like everything

@topic solo_vs_group
@levels 1-50
@scene solo_or_group
@role B type=Leveler
@role C type=Socialite
@role D type=Daredevil
A: do you prefer solo or group leveling?
B: group, the xp is better and the time goes faster
C: group, but only with people who talk
D: solo, nobody blames me when it goes wrong
B: nobody saves you either
D: that is half the thrill
A: groups for me, i need the company
